WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:04.300
This is the second son of 
a mold-starter business owner,

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.480
who just started at the Agricultural 
University this spring,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.980
Sawaki Souemon Tadayasu-kun.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.550
He has the ability to see 
microbes with the naked eye.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:10.730
A.   oryzae

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.490
S.   lactis  

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:12.990
A.   aceti

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.990
Amazing, isn't it?

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.670
Moyashimon

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.450
This is great!

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.200
If you're Japanese, 
you've gotta love miso soup and rice!

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.210
These pickles are so good!

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.500
Mutou was one of the 
best-looking girls on campus.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.640
They even called her 
"Miss Agricultural University."

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.480
I thought we hadn't seen her in a while,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.630
These rice balls are so good!

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.370
but to think she's been reduced to this...

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.990
Though, girls at this 
school wear less makeup

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.930
with each passing year.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:09.060
I'm impressed she can eat 
with the smell in here.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.170
Who is this girl?

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.040
Enchanting! 
Miss Agricultural University

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.790
Mutou-kun, why did you take so long?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.410
I went all the way to the 
other side of the world

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.360
to help Haruka-san with her research.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.510
Then I ended up stockpiling a 
bunch of fermented goods...

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.180
Bye.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.220
What?!

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.590
And when it came time 
to go back to Japan,

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.270
Haruka-san said I had 
to travel by land.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.160
The fermented stuff would explode

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.780
from the air pressure in an airplane.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.270
Hi!

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.300
Oh, Chinese?

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.700
Then, since I was traveling by land,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.030
Oh, Chinese!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.300
I bought a few more 
things along the way.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.490
That was cruel.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.390
I couldn't help it!

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.500
Something came up and 
I had to hurry back.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.760
It was a good experience, though.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:23.970
Mutou-kun, may I look in your bag?

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.220
Oh, that's right! 
It needs to be chilled, quick!

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.250
There's fermented fish and meat

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.320
and all kinds of stuff in there.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.230
The smell is remarkable.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.480
Well, half of that might be me.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.080
As of two weeks ago, I'd been wearing

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.990
this outfit for two weeks.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.290
Apparently girls can get 
used to being filthy, too.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.490
I don't know about that.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.500
Yuuki-kun, would you 
help me carry these?

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:52.300
Sure.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.750
Mutou-kun, take some time 
to recover from your trip.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.400
Okay, I'll go use the showers 
in my friend's athletic club.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.460
At last, I get to see 
fresh water again!

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.260
Hey, hey, hey!

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.880
It's way too cold!

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.390
Let's get inside a human!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.670
What is it, Sawaki?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.360
It's just... there are some 
nasty-looking guys on this.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.750
This looks like kumis.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.180
It didn't explode even 
in a canteen like this,

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.170
since it's made with 
weaker fermentation.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.960
All three of the Surströmming 
cans are pushing their limits.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.880
We should eat those with the others soon.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.100
Yes.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:50.760
What did you think of the 
sake Kikuji-san gave you?

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.250
Well...

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.680
The filtering process was different

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.650
from ordinary unpasteurized sake.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.300
The fragrance was completely 
different from types

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.870
of sake that are ultra-filtered

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.800
so they can be stored 
at room temperature.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.540
Why did such a rustic bar have that?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.610
You're that curious about his bar?

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:12.410
Well, no...

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.780
Still, what a waste.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.170
I hate to bring it up again, but...

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.000
You are right, though.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.650
But it's something I had decided

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.260
before I entered this school.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.540
Well, it's good to have 
something you want to do.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.140
And when do you start?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.880
I've already prepared my request 
for leave from school.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.770
I'll start my break when 
the time is right.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.660
Um, Hasegawa-san...

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.790
Wh-What kind of microbes were they?

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:04.300
Why didn't you speak 
up sooner, Sawaki?!

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:08.940
Asia's top five food poisoning 
microbes are in this room!

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.050
Are you serious?!

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.500
Don't spray the equipment directly!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.880
Got it, Researcher Hasegawa!

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.230
Whiskers! Fatso! Cover more consistently!

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.070
What are you guys doing?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.200
Oh, Hasegawa-san, it's Mutou-san.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.700
Where have you been?

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.150
Taking a shower.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:38.120
One of the cheerleaders 
let me borrow a uniform.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.160
And since it's a new school year,

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.130
I bought a new lab coat 
at the co-op store.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.620
I finally got to wash off the 
grime from my long trip!

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.510
I feel totally refreshed!

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:51.460
Okay, Haruka-san,

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.330
I'll just pop in to visit 
my club and head home.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.890
Hold it right there, Mutou.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.290
Sawaki.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:00.890
Right.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.660
Showering doesn't get all the germs off.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.650
Look closely.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.650
A-Are you saying I'm 
carrying some disease?

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:16.410
Hello!

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.100
There's one!

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.290
Commence disinfection!

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.570
Mutou-san...

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.550
Don't hate us.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.710
We'll ask the real disinfection team

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.360
to treat the co-op store and showers.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:53.610
Sorry... I'm really sorry about this!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.620
Ishikawa General Hospital

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.520
She really is a handful.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.980
What's with that getup?

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.080
H-How'd it go?

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.580
The official results aren't back yet,

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:11.090
but I have no symptoms. 
Looks like I'm fine.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.110
Slime molds are really amazing...

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.170
Yeah.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:18.720
It actually chose the shortest 
of the three possible routes.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.790
Good thing I covered it before

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.600
we went to that liquor store.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.220
I thought that disinfection 
earlier had killed them.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.120
Good job, Kawahama!

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.230
You guys are still playing with that?

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.110
If you have nothing 
to do, then go home.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.830
Why should we?

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.490
We're waiting for the other two.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:42.680
Then would you guys give Mutou

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:44.000
her welcome back party?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.390
She likes to drink,

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.220
so take her to a pub or something.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.000
Okay.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.630
But you're not coming, Hasegawa-san?

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:55.880
I... can't drink alcohol.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.890
After she made us do all that work...

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.470
A girl with that kind of personality 
who can't even drink...

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.270
No guy is ever gonna 
make a move on her.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.560
So you really can see microbes.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.930
I couldn't believe it when the 
professor told me last year.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.540
Yeah, well...

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.670
Hey, can that girly-looking 
boy see them, too?

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.920
Calling Kei girly-looking is taboo.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.650
Oh, it's Mutou.

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:38.110
Wow, it is! I haven't seen her in ages!

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.750
Who's that guy in the front?

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.180
It's that first-year.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.350
Notice and Warning of Herbicide Testing

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.350
This 
Year's 
Offenders

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.350
Agricultural Dept.  1st Year  
Sawaki Tadayasu-kun

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.350
Agricultural Dept.  1st Year  
Yuuki Kei-kun

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.350
The one who was on the bulletin 
board for stealing vegetables.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:45.800
Hey, it's Mutou!

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.350
Is that Sawaki?

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:51.390
You're pretty popular, Mutou-san.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:54.480
Sounds like you're rather 
well-known yourself.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.610
It's more like infamy in my case.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.490
Don't worry about it.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:01.620
Being popular incorporates 
the good and the bad.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.120
Tennis

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.120
Anime

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:07.040
I've never been to the 
club building before.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.780
Then you might as well check out

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.630
what the clubs are like while you're here.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:14.130
I don't know if my club's 
members will be here, though.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.930
Isn't it kind of smoky in here?

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:26.730
Is it?

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.530
I can't really tell.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:33.520
Which means it's microbes again...

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.030
What's wrong, Sawaki-kun?

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.960
Asia's 
Top 
5

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.640
Wh-What were these guys again?

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.970
Here it is, Sawaki-kun. Come on.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.730
Research Club

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:09.730
UFO research club?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.550
That's right. I'm the president.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:15.020
I was convinced you were a cheerleader.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.980
I told you, I just borrowed 
the uniform from a friend.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.510
Are you guys in here?

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:24.370
Maybe they're aliens...

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.590
Ugh, it's humid!

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.380
What are you guys doing?

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:38.250
Oh, President!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.930
It's Mutou-san! Wake up!

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.880
What are you doing, 
all shut up in here?

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.260
It's the end of April!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.860
Oh...

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.640
Now I remember. It's influenza.

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:52.890
Huh? Influenza?

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:55.220
And a lot of it.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.770
You'll catch it if you don't 
put a mask on, Mutou-san.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:01.280
W-We all caught it, one by one.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.690
None of us have any money,

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.660
so we've been living in here, 
helping each other out.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.550
Influenza outbreaks stop 
when April ends, right?

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:12.440
If we hang in there until 
the cherry blossoms fall,

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.790
we can overcome this.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:15.900
The heater is fine,

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:19.420
but this dry air is like 
paradise for influenza!

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:24.550
Wh-What are these?

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.680
You have to ask?

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.690
They're chickens and pigs.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.660
The chickens are for eggs,

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.120
and we borrowed the pigs from Livestock

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.560
to cheer ourselves up.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.990
It's weird, though.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:39.320
All the chickens we borrowed 
from Livestock died.

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.670
We secretly bought 
these to replace them.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:43.290
Right?

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.320
Wh-Why chickens and pigs?

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:51.160
Aren't you guys in any groups 
that study microorganisms?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.040
Or is this some kind of 
happy-go-lucky group suicide?!

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:57.650
Pigs are susceptible to both 
human flu and bird flu!

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:59.190
They act as intermediates!

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:02.050
These are the perfect conditions 
for breeding new strains!

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.890
R-Really?

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.910
I knew something wasn't right!

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.930
This is my second time 
getting the flu this year!

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:10.930
Sawaki-kun, call the disinfection team.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.400
They're probably still out 
there sanitizing stuff.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.800
Come on, you guys, get up!

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.190
Uh... right...

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.490
Now there's a new strain 
of influenza on campus?

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.540
What a pain...

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.140
Yeah.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.400
What are those UFO guys doing?

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:28.920
Everyone, please vacate the premises!

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:30.200
We're closing down the club building!

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.580
Get all the UFO club 
members to the hospital!

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:42.840
They might as well just 
burn down the building.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.600
Sorry this keeps piling up.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.840
Everywhere you go is 
infested with microbes.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:50.350
<i>She has a point.</i>

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.180
Sawaki, that mask is pointless.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.920
Influenza can get 
through regular masks.

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:57.940
It can?

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.110
Masks don't keep viruses out.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.320
The humidity trapped 
in them from your breath

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.940
just stops viruses that like 
dry air for a little while.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.570
Curses! The humidity is stopping us!

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:14.080
It's Hasegawa and Mutou!

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:17.810
If you two start to feel 
sick, get to the hospital.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.330
Don't forget, people die from influenza.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.480
As Professor Itsuki would say,

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:27.020
it's mankind's smallest 
and most powerful enemy.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.780
Wahoo!

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.610
Our first time drinking with a girl!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.440
College is awesome!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.190
Come on, let's go!

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.530
Hey, Sawaki-kun and I 
might have influenza.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.820
We can't overdo it.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:49.570
I wonder if Kei went home...

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:52.950
The fermenting cellar was 
empty and closed up, too.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:15:03.840
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.540
See, Kawahama? It's closed.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:01.100
This place always closes by six.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.510
Well, I thought the standing bar 
we visited during the day

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:05.320
would be open at night, too.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:07.460
Want to go to a bar I know, then?

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.720
The girl I borrowed the 
cheerleader outfit from

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.150
works there part-time.

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:13.640
Sorry... we always drink in our dorm,

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.470
so we don't know much 
about what's out here.

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:19.600
But there are a lot of cars 
parked in front of this store.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.860
It's always like that around here.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.960
They're all fancy-looking cars.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.430
Creepy.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.990
Well, if it isn't Mutou. Welcome.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:34.400
I'll return your outfit after I wash it.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:37.120
What, you're not here 
with the UFO club today?

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.500
These guys are Professor 
Itsuki's pre-seminar students.

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:44.380
Ah, then will that high and 
mighty princess be joining you?

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.560
Oh, yeah... Where's Haruka-san?

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.510
Maybe she'll come once the 
disinfecting is finished.

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:53.010
Hasegawa-san said she 
can't drink alcohol.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.770
Well, I guess we can't help that...

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.620
Anyway, have a seat.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:04.270
This isn't a standing bar.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:09.890
I'm Hirooka Aya, a third-year 
in agroeconomics.

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:11.540
We don't have many customers

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.280
since it's a weekday, so drink all you like.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.020
Thanks.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:17.280
Want to start with a round of beers?

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:20.440
Oh, he and I are underage,

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.040
so if you have juice or something...

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.280
What did you do at the UFO club?

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.540
Why did you join?

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.920
Well... see...

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:35.050
They look for UFOs.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:39.060
Mutou had a boyfriend before 
she started at the university.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.560
Remember to watch your step!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.060
Right!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.730
He wanted to live together,

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.810
so Mutou worked day and night.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:52.510
She worked so hard, 
it was painful to watch.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.070
He took charge of all 
the money she earned

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.690
and put it in savings.

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:00.580
Mutou spent every day dreaming

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.970
about the happiness yet to come.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:08.170
But then one day, 
when she visited his place...

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.840
To Aoi

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:16.430
I fell in love with someone else.

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.590
That's weird...

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:22.790
Mutou figured he must have 
been abducted by aliens,

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:25.440
and that's what brought her 
knocking at the UFO club's door.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.440
Bombay on the rocks.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.090
That's just running away 
from reality, isn't it?

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:44.950
Well, there are many strange 
things in this world.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.760
Yay!

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:52.510
I see... a fermenting cellar, huh?

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.330
You've got it rough 
right from year one.

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:56.660
Yeah, if I'm going to 
be part of it anyway,

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:59.500
I'd rather learn about good sake.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.100
You mean really fancy, top-grade sake,

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:06.600
or legendary sake that's hard to find?

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:09.720
I'm not sure how to put it...

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:12.950
But I guess I think of it as sake that

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:15.110
makes you feel the pride of the brewer.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.320
Pride, huh?

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.990
That's a little different 
from how I see it.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.480
I think all sake,

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:26.310
whether it's made by a big 
company or a small brewery,

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:29.370
is made with pride, regardless of 
whether they love or hate the taste.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:32.130
I'm only working here part-time,

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:35.180
but I always clean up the 
beer tap before we open.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:38.880
There's no need to do that every day,

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:42.180
but if the flavor was affected 
at all because of me,

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.010
it's an injustice to 
whoever made the beer.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:49.890
Otherwise, I just work hard so 
the people who chose our bar

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:54.220
can enjoy themselves and 
go home nice and drunk.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:59.100
Whatever you decide to do 
while you're on leave,

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:01.640
the school gate will always be open.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:04.040
This may be a good 
opportunity for Sawaki-kun

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:06.540
to start relying on himself, as well.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.040
Where are we going, Professor?

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.370
You wouldn't even tell the others.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:15.850
To make you want to return 
from your break sooner,

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:18.800
I'm going to show you my secret place.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:28.430
I've come from Hiyoshi's 
night bar to pick you up.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:33.500
I'm better at darts.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:34.380
Shut up.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.790
It's only because you stopped 
drinking halfway through.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.860
Look, a UFO!

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:42.200
You said you'd go easy on 
the alcohol tonight...

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:46.930
It's impossible for her to go 
easy on alcohol, Hazuki-chan.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:51.700
What's going on? 
I can't reach Kei's phone.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.960
Sawaki-kun!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.450
You'll get left behind!

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:56.830
Oh, sorry!

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.510
Moyashimon

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.510
Episode 6

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.510
Microbe Theater

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.510
Microbe Theater 6!

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:31.180
A-Are you saying I'm 
carrying some disease?

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:36.170
I shouldn't bother introducing 
myself to the likes of you...

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:39.590
Osaka University Professor 
Fujino Tsunesaburou

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:37.370
But I'm Vibrio parahaemolyticus,

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.390
discovered by Professor Fujino 
Tsunesaburou of Osaka University.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:44.030
Vibrio 
parahaemolyticus  
Named in 1951

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:44.030
I like to live on raw seafood!

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:47.530
Next, I'm El Tor cholera.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.710
The same cholera you're 
all familiar with,

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:53.270
V. cholerae  
El Tor Cholera  
Discovered in 1884

00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:53.290
but I'm the latest strain 
that's going around recently!

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.870
Next, I'm bacterial 
dysentery, Shigella.

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:57.870
S. dysenteriae  
Shigella  
Discovered in 1897

00:21:57.870 --> 00:22:00.360
Medical Scientist  
Shiga Kiyoshi

00:21:57.870 --> 00:22:00.380
I'm called Shigella because 
I was discovered by

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:03.300
the medical scientist Shiga Kiyoshi.

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:05.820
And I'm P. shigelloides.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:08.470
You can catch me by 
drinking unboiled water!

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:08.470
P. shigelloides  
Present in Freshwater Environments  
Discovered in 1947

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:11.980
Finally, I'm salmonella.

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:15.470
Salmonella Bacteria  
Named in 1885

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:14.860
I have more than 2,000 buddies 
who can invade your intestines!

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:18.230
We're...

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:21.050
Asia's top five food poisoning microbes!

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:24.980
Asia's Top Five Food Poisoning Microbes

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:22.550
Commence disinfection!

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:29.950
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 7,

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:29.950
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:34.790
Next Week: 
"The Agricultural University 
Spring Festival Begins!"

00:22:30.190 --> 00:22:34.210
Sawaki-kun, how many years have 
you not had a girlfriend?
